m its recorded claim to its reviewed tip; iteration rounds between full rounds review only rework since the last reviewed state, answer that round's findings, and never clear integration, whether their session was started fresh or resumed.\"","+requirement = \"The delivered loop content shall, when unattended work reaches integration, obtain each review or critique verdict the declared policy requires from a session that did not author the work — resolved per in-process phase and tier from the delivered agent registry's declared (family x model x tier) rows and only while the declared consent surface that turns managed selection on is present, drawn from a different model family wherever one is configured, degrading only to the documented same-family mode — with every selection logged before launch and a non-converging rework loop escalated through the declared approval level, and, where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, refuse build output at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when.\"","+rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-026 (cross-family second opinions — every prior carrier of this contract demoted as routing machinery, so the sn_refs join forced the mint; SR-155 cites SN-026 too, for the planner pair, but only this row states the second opinion itself), SN-024 (an author cannot judge its own output) and SN-006. One row because routing, scheduling, scoring and escalation are one delivered contract — that the second opinion happens, independently, or its absence is documented — whose mechanics are the component details below it. The row also carries SN-026's DECLARATION and CONSENT half — `docs/agents.toml`'s pair-rows and the `docs/agents-enabled` surface whose presence turns managed selection on. That half had ZERO textual occurrence anywhere in the SR layer while `orphans=0` still held, because an orphan count proves a need has a citing row and never that the row carries the whole need. Managed selection is opt-in by consent rather than by configuration alone: a repository that declares families without dropping the surface has declared a capability, not turned one on, and the row now says so where a check can read it. fan-out re-stamp: the single plan's independent critique is one obligation carried by its briefs and filing and by its gate; the routing children remain separate.\"\"\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"A declared review policy of N schedules N independent reviewer sessions; the declared (family x model x tier) pair-rows of the delivered agent registry are the only candidate source, and the declared consent surface's presence is what turns managed selection on — absent, managed selection is off and no row is resolved; present, exactly one row resolves per in-process phase and tier; a configured cross-family draw is preferred and its unavailability degrades to the documented mode, never a silent skip; every selection is logged before launch, never a silent model swap; rework iterates within the declared budget and pages per the declared approval level on exhaustion. The verdict that may clear integration comes from a session minted for that review, or, where reviewer retention is on and the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, from a round the coordinator recorded as final for the lane's retained final reviewer, over the whole lane, from its recorded claim to its reviewed tip; iteration rounds between full rounds review only rework since the last reviewed state, answer that round's findings, and never clear integration, whether their session was started fresh or resumed. Where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, no build output is accepted at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when; the plan either covers every Done-when item or excludes it with a reason, declares an architectural delta of none, or one carried within its scope. One revision receives a fresh independent critique. If that second critique does not read as an approval, only an accepted dispute dismissal of every blocking or major finding permits the record; otherwise the item goes to the owner. A plan or Done-when changed after the record requires a fresh record. Ticking a Done-when item, or adding evidence to it, does not require a fresh record. Work items whose plan mark is absent, empty, none or dual are not held by this planning requirement; an unrecognized mark is held.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-913\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3390,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3390,"newLines":7,"lines":[" verifies = [\"SR-146\", \"SR-154\", \"SR-235\", \"LLR-313\", \"IF-046\", \"IF-047\", \"IF-288\", \"IF-289\"]"," level = \"Integration\""," method = \"Run test_a_rendered_review_brief_carries_the_kit_clauses_and_the_lane_facts, test_a_narrow_round_names_the_findings_it_answers, test_a_narrow_round_without_findings_and_a_full_one_with_them_are_refused, test_a_named_input_that_is_not_there_refuses, test_an_unfilled_slot_refuses_and_no_brief_is_written, test_the_scope_critique_carries_ruling_twos_questions_and_its_rubric, test_a_filed_coordinator_review_appears_in_the_rollup, test_a_bracketed_word_that_is_not_a_severity_never_refuses_a_filing, test_a_malformed_review_is_refused_and_nothing_is_filed, test_a_round_with_no_tests_refuses, test_an_empty_or_missing_named_input_refuses, test_the_critique_render_refuses_a_missing_spec, test_the_command_line_refuses_a_lane_the_git_reads_reject, test_a_review_render_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_brief, and test_filing_a_review_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_round_file. Render full and narrow review briefs and a scope critique over a temporary lane; refuse an empty test list, empty or missing named inputs, and a critique without a specification; on a real lane, drive detached, non-commit and non-ancestor command-line refusals, then successful review rendering and filing; file a well-formed review and malformed review cases, including a non-severity bracketed bullet beside a matching declared finding count, and attempt filing for a lane whose branch the round reader cannot read back as a review scope or whose branch names the rollup generator's own directory, before rendering the rollup. Per commit, render the first and revised single-plan briefs and exercise their missing-input and unfilled-slot refusals. Only in the full suite, exercise plan-critique rendering, filing, the pass form and their refusals, including a MINOR before a MAJOR with dismissal of F2, two blocking findings with only one dismissed, a revision that misses a first finding, and a committed critique whose working copy differs only by line-ending conversion or has a real uncommitted edit.\"","-tier = \"Smoke\"","+tier = \"Full\""," expected = \"A complete attended review or critique brief has no unfilled slot and carries the shipped review clauses, lane facts or scope rubric as applicable. An empty test list, invalid round shape, missing specification, unreadable or empty named input, unfilled template slot, malformed or unbound verdict (without exactly one line whose keyword, compared case-insensitively, is VERDICT in the canonical form `VERDICT: <APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED> findings=<digits>`), a lane branch the round reader cannot read as a review scope, and a lane whose scope is the rollup generator's own directory are refused without a requested file or review record. A bracketed non-severity bullet beside N declared-severity findings and findings=N is filed, and its rollup shows N. A detached lane, non-commit revision or non-ancestor base returns exit 2 with no output file and a clean repository. A successful review returns exit 0 and writes only its brief with full resolved revisions and the reviewed tip; successful filing returns exit 0 and adds only the next review-round record. A valid filed review is rendered in the lane review history. Per-commit brief renders and their stated refusals remain in the smoke tier. The full suite proves that the first critique covers Done-when alone, the second also covers first-critique finding identifiers without their text, a revision missing a first finding is refused at render, a MINOR before a MAJOR passes on dismissal of F2, two blocking findings with only one dismissed are refused, and a committed critique changed only by line-ending conversion passes while a real uncommitted edit is refused. The second plan critique's brief never carries the first critique's verdict or any finding's text. A successfully filed critique writes only its record. A plan critique with a missing rubric, plan or specification, or a beyond delta, refuses without output. The shipped planner template is in the catalogue and names no skill or repository row.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_rendered_review_brief_carries_the_kit_clauses_and_the_lane_facts; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_narrow_round_names_the_findings_it_answers; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_narrow_round_without_findings_and_a_full_one_with_them_are_refused; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_named_input_that_is_not_there_refuses; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_an_unfilled_slot_refuses_and_no_brief_is_written; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_the_scope_critique_carries_ruling_twos_questions_and_its_rubric; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_filed_coordinator_review_appears_in_the_rollup; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_bracketed_word_that_is_not_a_severity_never_refuses_a_filing; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_malformed_review_is_refused_and_nothing_is_filed; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_round_with_no_tests_refuses; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_an_empty_or_missing_named_input_refuses; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_the_critique_render_refuses_a_missing_spec; tests/test_review_brief_git.py::test_the_command_line_refuses_a_